 {
  "id": "e:kalde på|phrase#1",
  "kind": "example",
  "unit": "entry:kalde på|phrase",
  "passed": false,
  "stage": "review",
  "problems": [
   "sense: 'kalder på' means to call out to someone to get their attention, not to call by phone. The Danish sentence implies calling out, but the translations use 'позвоню'/'подзвоню'/'call' (by phone), which does not match the Danish meaning.",
   "The Danish sentence 'Jeg kalder på dig når maden er færdig' means 'I call you when the food is ready' (shouting or calling out to someone), but the Russian translation 'Я позвоню, когда еда будет готова' and Ukrainian translation 'Я подзвоню, коли їжа буде готова' mean 'I will call (by phone) when the food is ready', which is a different meaning."
  ]
 },
